          </h3>
          <p>
            To receive the maximum spiritual resonance from your daily recitation, tradition recommends reciting during <strong>Brahma Muhurat</strong> (approximately 4:00 AM to 5:30 AM before sunrise) or during evening Sandhya hours at dusk. Devotees should cleanse themselves with a bath, sit facing East or North on a clean wool or kusha grass mat (aasan), and illuminate a brass diya with pure cow ghee or sesame (til) oil.
          </p>
          <p>
            It is auspicious to begin every chanting session by remembering Bhagwan Shri Ram Chandra and Mother Sita, as Lord Hanuman is perpetually present wherever the holy name of Rama is uttered with devotion. Depending on one&apos;s daily vows (sankalpa), the Chalisa may be chanted 1, 3, 7, 11, or 100 times (Shatpath). For detailed rules on pronunciation, sankalpa guidelines, Tuesday-Saturday fasting, and deity offerings, refer to our complete <a href="/shri-hanuman-chalisa-path-vidhi" class="text-vermilion underline font-bold hover:text-marigold transition-colors">Hanuman Chalisa Path Vidhi Guide</a>.
